d1589578246ad9d7da279b4397fd4d2bf4f42ed7
read: blind Terra cold read of the land tools' diff (land-train, ci-verdict, e2e-shards, burst-bisect, evergreen-boundary) = HOLD: P1 a &#45;-poll/&#45;-interval past Node's timer limit (2147484 s) clamped to 1 ms and slipped under the pace — cured red-first at 4d439f2e8 (pollRefusal refuses poll-over-timer-limit for both tools); P1-b consecutive gh calls inside one verdict round — ruled a wording fix (the law spaces ROUNDS of reads, never calls within a round), trued in headers, comments and test names; P2 the find budget's injected now() hid its Date.now from the evergreen witness — the witness now flags a now = Date.now default, and two named own-liveness exceptions account for it (the budget decides only the tool's own giving-up, allowed under the no-global-now ruling). The stale e2e-shards clock exception left by the find-loop change cured at 91a88466a. CI 42144178193 green at this head (the span a9f461bf4 merged in).

<<~/ahu>>

